// Interprocedural Call-Site Constant/Closure Specialization & Tail-Call Optimization (T614 / E15.4).
// Implements SPEC-73 §§5, 7, 8, 9 (AXS-INL-027..031, AXS-INL-033, AXS-INL-034, AXS-INL-035;
// REQ-OPT-002..003, REQ-OPT-087..102):
//   - Canonical `SpecializationKey` & deterministic clone symbol mangling (`AXS-INL-028`, `AXS-INL-030`)
//   - Representation-equivalent code sharing with strict function-pointer identity preservation (`AXS-INL-029`, `REQ-OPT-098..099`)
//   - Partial call-site constant, enum-tag, and closure specialization with `SpecializationBudget`
//     (`max_clones_per_fn`, `max_module_growth_pct`, `min_benefit_score`) and post-specialization
//     `ConstFold` + `SROA` + `SimplifyCFG` + `DCE` cleanup + summary refinement (`AXS-INL-030..031`)
//   - Tail-call & self-tail-recursion optimization (`TCO_LEGAL` preconditions: zero post-call `Drop`
//     glue, zero stack-borrowed `view<T>`/`mut_view<T>`/pointers escaping to callee, no post-call
//     volatile/atomic barrier; `O(1)` stack self-tail-recursion loop lowering, sibling tail-call
//     qualification, and explicit `@tailcall` legality verification) (`AXS-INL-033`, `REQ-OPT-002..003`)
//   - `PassManager` `TransformationContract`s (`PASS_IPA_SPECIALIZE = 15u16`, `PASS_TAILCALL = 17u16`) (`AXS-INL-034`)
//   - Deterministic `--emit=specialize` (`ipa_specialize_print`) and `--emit=inline` TCO (`ipa_tailcall_print`) (`AXS-INL-035`)
module compiler.opt.ipa

